1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:09,844
You wake up, and the first thing you see is your cat, Biscuit, staring at you. That's normal. She does that every morning. But today, you hear something.

2
00:00:10,194 --> 00:00:13,184
If he doesn't feed me in three minutes, the glass goes on the floor.

3
00:00:14,084 --> 00:00:18,645
You look around. No one else is here. Just you... and the cat.

4
00:00:18,995 --> 00:00:19,642
Two minutes.

5
00:00:21,392 --> 00:00:31,339
You don't know what's happening yet. But by the end of this week, you'll find out what every animal in your life really thinks about you. And one of them has been keeping a secret for years.

6
00:00:35,839 --> 00:00:39,607
In the kitchen, your dog Max runs in so fast he slides into the fridge.

7
00:00:39,957 --> 00:00:49,770
BEST DAY EVER! BEST DAY EVER! ...Also, yesterday was the best day ever. Every day is the best day ever!

8
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:51,590
Okay. That one makes sense.

9
00:00:52,490 --> 00:00:54,974
Who's a good boy? Who's the best boy in the world?

10
00:00:55,324 --> 00:01:01,283
ME! It's me! I'm the good boy! ...Wait, is there another dog? Is HE the good boy?

11
00:01:01,633 --> 00:01:05,602
Max spins around three times looking for the other dog. There is no other dog.

12
00:01:06,502 --> 00:01:08,082
Hello! Hello! Pretty bird!

13
00:01:08,432 --> 00:01:11,615
I know exactly what I'm saying. I just like watching them get excited.

14
00:01:11,965 --> 00:01:14,569
Even the parrot next door is smarter than he looks.

15
00:01:15,469 --> 00:01:20,749
Whoa, a castle! ...Whoa, a castle! ...Whoa, a castle!

16
00:01:21,099 --> 00:01:25,349
So it's true. Goldfish really do forget everything in three seconds.

17
00:01:26,249 --> 00:01:30,814
You need to be sure you're not going crazy. So you kneel down next to Biscuit and whisper,

18
00:01:31,164 --> 00:01:32,111
Can you understand me?

19
00:01:32,461 --> 00:01:34,317
Obviously. I'm just ignoring you.

20
00:01:34,667 --> 00:01:39,376
Great. Your cat has been understanding you this whole time. She just doesn't care.

21
00:01:40,276 --> 00:01:43,961
You take Max for a walk, and the park is suddenly very, very loud.

22
00:01:44,861 --> 00:01:48,251
That man's shoes smell like cheese. Ten out of ten.

23
00:01:48,601 --> 00:01:53,707
I am a wolf. I am a wolf. I am a... is that a leaf?

24
00:01:54,607 --> 00:01:55,124
SQUIRREL!

25
00:01:58,007 --> 00:02:02,420
He doesn't laugh anymore. I bring him the ball every day. Maybe tomorrow he'll laugh.

26
00:02:02,770 --> 00:02:09,660
And for a second, the park doesn't feel funny anymore. Some of these thoughts are jokes. Some of them aren't.

27
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:13,205
On a bench, a group of pigeons is watching people eat.

28
00:02:13,555 --> 00:02:17,047
Okay, the guy with the sandwich. On three, we all look sad.

29
00:02:17,397 --> 00:02:22,833
It works. He gives them half his sandwich. That night, you write down everything you know.

30
00:02:29,133 --> 00:02:35,968
The next day, you decide to use your power for good. Your neighbor, Mrs. Lee, is worried. Her dog won't eat.

31
00:02:36,318 --> 00:02:39,759
He hasn't touched his food in three days. I don't know what's wrong.

32
00:02:40,659 --> 00:02:44,278
There's a scary dog living in my new bowl. He copies everything I do.

33
00:02:44,628 --> 00:02:50,840
It's his reflection. You swap the shiny bowl for an old one. He eats everything in ten seconds.

34
00:02:51,740 --> 00:03:05,007
By the weekend, you're the neighborhood pet expert. A parrot that won't stop screaming? He's bored. He wants a new toy. A cat that keeps hiding? She hates the new vacuum cleaner. And honestly, so do you.

35
00:03:05,907 --> 00:03:10,145
A little girl brings you her rabbit. She says he keeps barking. Rabbits don't bark.

36
00:03:10,495 --> 00:03:14,192
I live with three dogs. I am also a dog. Woof.

37
00:03:14,542 --> 00:03:15,759
You decide not to tell him.

38
00:03:16,659 --> 00:03:23,351
Even Max has a secret. Every day, he barks at the mailman like a monster. Everyone thinks he hates him.

39
00:03:23,701 --> 00:03:30,021
HI! HI! I LOVE YOU! PLEASE PET ME! WHY DO YOU ALWAYS RUN AWAY?!

40
00:03:30,921 --> 00:03:34,209
He doesn't hate the mailman. He's in love with the mailman.

41
00:03:34,559 --> 00:03:38,630
Huh. Fifteen years on this street, and nobody's dog has ever liked me.

42
00:03:38,980 --> 00:03:41,741
He laughs. It's the first time you've ever seen him laugh.

43
00:03:42,641 --> 00:03:47,662
Then you visit Jay. He has a hamster named Nugget. And Nugget has a lot to say.

44
00:03:48,562 --> 00:03:56,757
Every night, he tells me about a girl. Mia. Mia this, Mia that. Mia laughed at my joke. I'm a hamster. I don't care.

45
00:03:57,657 --> 00:04:03,981
Mia. Your sister Mia. Your best friend has a crush on your sister. And the hamster knows everything.

46
00:04:04,881 --> 00:04:08,902
But there's a problem. Animals never stop thinking. Not even at night.

47
00:04:09,252 --> 00:04:11,923
Is that a bird? No, it's a bag.

48
00:04:12,273 --> 00:04:17,749
Running... running... the ball... so many balls...

49
00:04:18,099 --> 00:04:18,833
Whoa, a castle!

50
00:04:19,183 --> 00:04:24,328
You haven't slept properly in three days. And you're starting to learn things you really didn't need to know.

51
00:04:25,228 --> 00:04:26,301
And you can't help yourself.

52
00:04:26,651 --> 00:04:28,272
So... Mia, huh?

53
00:04:28,622 --> 00:04:31,279
Who told you that? I never told anyone. Only...

54
00:04:31,629 --> 00:04:32,300
...Only Nugget.

55
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:37,746
You try to explain. You can hear animals think. Jay stares at you for a long time.

56
00:04:38,096 --> 00:04:40,845
So you've been spying on me. Through my hamster.

57
00:04:41,195 --> 00:04:46,345
It's not like that! I didn't ask him! He just... thinks really loudly!

58
00:04:46,695 --> 00:04:50,856
Do you know how weird that sounds? Do you know how weird ALL of this sounds?

59
00:04:51,756 --> 00:04:54,406
Okay. When you say it like that, it sounds bad.

60
00:04:55,756 --> 00:05:06,000
On Sunday, you visit Grandma Rose. Her old dog, Pepper, walks next to her like always. Slowly. Carefully. Pepper is fourteen years old.

61
00:05:06,350 --> 00:05:08,548
Look at her. Still my best walking partner.

62
00:05:08,898 --> 00:05:16,136
Fourteen years, and she's never missed a single walk. Not one. Not even in the snow.

63
00:05:17,036 --> 00:05:19,122
Grandma smiles. And then you hear Pepper.

64
00:05:19,472 --> 00:05:25,292
My legs hurt. They hurt every day now. But Rose smiles when we walk together. So I walk.

65
00:05:26,192 --> 00:05:29,511
You look at Pepper. She's been hiding her pain. For Grandma.

66
00:05:29,861 --> 00:05:32,044
Don't tell her. She has enough to worry about.

67
00:05:32,394 --> 00:05:38,879
Last week, you learned that some secrets aren't yours to tell. But this one is different. This one is hurting someone.

68
00:05:39,779 --> 00:05:45,760
Grandma... I think Pepper's legs hurt. A lot. I think she's hiding it so you won't worry.

69
00:05:46,110 --> 00:05:50,512
Oh, Pepper. You silly old girl. You don't have to be strong for me.

70
00:05:50,862 --> 00:05:52,379
Yes, I do. That's my job.

71
00:05:53,279 --> 00:06:02,292
The vet says it's arthritis. Pepper gets medicine, a soft new bed, and shorter walks. A week later, she's walking better than she has in years.

72
00:06:03,192 --> 00:06:07,544
Thank you, kid. Don't tell Rose I said thanks. I have a reputation.

73
00:06:08,894 --> 00:06:10,285
Your hair looks like a broom.

74
00:06:10,635 --> 00:06:11,597
You call that singing?

75
00:06:11,947 --> 00:06:14,481
I'm sitting on your homework because your homework is wrong.

76
00:06:15,381 --> 00:06:27,103
Meanwhile, Biscuit has been insulting you all week. You're pretty sure she hates you. You're also pretty sure she's planning to replace you with the robot vacuum. She seems to like it more.

77
00:06:28,003 --> 00:06:35,321
Then, one night, you can't sleep. You keep your eyes closed. And you feel Biscuit climb onto your chest. Like she does every night.

78
00:06:36,221 --> 00:06:37,614
Still breathing. Good.

79
00:06:37,964 --> 00:06:44,925
I check every night. Ever since he got that fever when he was six. Nobody else was awake. I was.

80
00:06:45,825 --> 00:06:57,240
You remember that fever. You were six. Mom said the cat wouldn't leave your bed for three days. You always thought it was a funny story. Mom tells it at every family dinner. Nobody ever asked why the cat stayed.

81
00:06:58,140 --> 00:07:00,576
Silly human. Somebody has to watch you.

82
00:07:00,926 --> 00:07:10,294
You don't open your eyes. You don't say a word. But for the first time, you understand. Biscuit doesn't hate you. She's been guarding you your whole life.

83
00:07:12,044 --> 00:07:13,986
The next morning, you go to Jay's house.

84
00:07:14,336 --> 00:07:18,950
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have listened to Nugget. And I really shouldn't have said anything.

85
00:07:19,850 --> 00:07:22,758
Jay is quiet for a moment. Then he looks at the floor.

86
00:07:23,108 --> 00:07:24,777
...Did Nugget say if Mia likes me back?

87
00:07:25,127 --> 00:07:27,272
Nugget's a hamster, man. Ask her yourself.

88
00:07:28,172 --> 00:07:31,140
Finally. Maybe now he'll talk to HER instead of me.

89
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:39,820
Two days later, Jay finally does it. He walks up to Mia at the coffee shop. No hamster. No secret messages. Just Jay.

90
00:07:40,170 --> 00:07:43,077
Hey, Mia. Do you... maybe want to get pizza sometime?

91
00:07:43,427 --> 00:07:44,188
Took you long enough.

92
00:07:45,088 --> 00:07:49,945
At home, you feed Biscuit. Right on time. She takes one bite and looks up at you.

93
00:07:50,295 --> 00:07:50,957
Acceptable.

94
00:07:51,307 --> 00:07:53,632
From Biscuit, that's basically "I love you."

95
00:07:54,532 --> 00:07:59,341
That evening, Biscuit jumps onto the couch and stares at you. A long, slow stare.

96
00:07:59,691 --> 00:08:01,231
So. You can hear us now.

97
00:08:01,581 --> 00:08:04,602
Don't look so surprised. We've always been able to hear YOU.

98
00:08:05,502 --> 00:08:12,251
Every song you sing in the shower. Every time you talk to yourself. Every time you said you'd clean your room.

99
00:08:12,601 --> 00:08:13,320
We heard all of it.

100
00:08:14,870 --> 00:08:22,841
So here's the question. If you could hear what your pet really thinks... would you want to know? Or are some thoughts better left unheard?

